> This program is designed for endocrin[ologists, diabetes] and metabolism[ specialists], family[ medicine physicians], intern[ists,] physician[ assistants],[ nurse practitioners], nurses[,] dietit[ians] and other interested professionals.
The last[ few] years have witnessed some of the greatest breakthroughs[ in diabetes management since] the discovery of insulin[.] We have gone from two classes[ of] drugs for glycemic control to 14 classes[.] Gluco-centricity is also being placed in its correct perspective and personalized[ medicine] has replaced it with a multifactorial regimen[,] addressing the complexity of risk that accompanies[ diabetes.] For the first time[ we] have real compounds that reduce cardiovascular[ events and] even combat congest[ive] heart[ failure]. There is now a new recognition of the relationship[ between hypertension] and[ renal dysfunction] that[ compromises cardiac] function[. We] have finally conceded[ that] insulin[ resistance should] surrender its crown[ and that the] central role[ of] beta cell[ function] be given the recognition it deserves[.] Please join us for this one day[ diabetes] conference at Eastern Virginia[ Medical School].[][]

